; status: works — the rabbit-ear base [hull2020, Thm 8.5]. Three angle bisectors
; of a triangle meet at the incenter O; folding them plus the altitude from O to
; the base flat-collapses the single vertex (Kawasaki + Maekawa hold there).

paper square

; isoceles triangle a, b, m — m is the midpoint of the top edge
--v = map .a onto .b          ; x = 1/2: perp bisector of the base, also the spine
.m = --v * --cd               ; apex (1/2, 1)

step precrease
--am = through .a .m          ; TODO(pinch): landmark — replace with pinch when shipped
--bm = through .b .m          ; TODO(pinch): landmark — replace with pinch when shipped
--ba = map --ab onto --am     ; angle bisector at a (interior — filter picks it)
--bb = map --ab onto --bm     ; angle bisector at b
.o = --ba * --bb              ; incenter — the collapse vertex

step ear
; four creases through O: the a- and b-bisectors, the spine above O (third
; bisector, valley), and the altitude below O (the ear, mountain). `&` splits
; each material line at O into the one ray that reaches the vertex.
; the emitted FOLD edges_assignment is GLOBAL-frame M/V (spec §4.6, derived
; assignment = valley XOR the cutting face is back-up): the two --v rays lie
; on back-up sectors, so their golden letters invert (spine valley → M, ear
; mountain → V); --ba and --bb keep their declared letters.
@collapse --ba & .a and --bb & .b
  and --v & .m and (--v & --ab mountain)
